      "rev_n_9_35b413_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_35b413_1",
        "node_id": "n_9_35b413",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: The previous approach checks if each row and column has constant values, which is incorrect. Instead, we need to ensure that the difference between corresponding elements in the same row and column is consistent across the entire grid. This means that for any pair of indices (i, j) and (k, l), the condition \\(c_{i,j} - c_{i,k} = c_{l,j} - c_{l,k}\\) must hold true. By verifying this condition for all pairs, we can confirm whether the grid can be expressed as a sum of two vectors.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-1623576952253176473",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_9_35b413_0",
